# b00t Pair Concept datum — autonomous agent maintainer + SME for subsystems
# 🤓 Issue #77: b00t pair — conceptual definition, roles, lifecycle, protocol
# schema: 1 | bump ONLY on field definition changes
# last_updated: 2026-05-08
#
# Defines the b00t Pair concept: an autonomous agent that operates as a
# maintainer and subject matter domain expert (SME) of a subsystem — a repo,
# directory, service, or bounded code domain.
#
# A b00t pair is the atomic unit of subsystem ownership in the b00t agent
# ecosystem. Every pair consists of two complementary agents who collectively
# own a subsystem: one MAINTAINS (drives changes) and one REVIEWS (validates
# quality). Pairs rotate on a schedule to distribute context and prevent
# single points of failure.
#
